--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: c0dc09dbaa30e694681d8e3582c8800f, type: 3}
  m_Name: WeeklyAdjustemntsTutorial
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  title: 
  speakingCharacters:
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 6f74c587975259d4f9962efdb1c258ff, type: 2}
    dialogueLines:
    - line: Oh, last time I forgot to tell you something. At the end of every week,
        the current state of my kingdom is made public - and, naturally, the people
        and their lives react to it.
      choices: []
      isFinalLine: 0
      nextSpeakerID: 0
    - line: 'Their loyalty <sprite name=Loyalty To King> towards me, my authority
        <sprite name=Authority> over them, population growth <sprite name=Population
        Growth>, interest of becoming a soldier <sprite name=Soldier Growth>... these
        are the usual things that shift when the current state is being published. '
      choices: []
      isFinalLine: 0
      nextSpeakerID: 0
    - line: 'These things get affected by how full my treasury <sprite name=Gold>
        is, if there is enough food <sprite name=Food> and how much gets produced
        <sprite name=Food Production>... also the size of my army <sprite name=Soldiers>
        and the general health <sprite name=Health> of the people. '
      choices:
      - conditionToShow: {fileID: 0}
        conditionToHide: {fileID: 0}
        choiceText: So, if the state of the kingdom is bad at the end of a week -
          it will get worse?
        responseToChoice: Generally, yeah. But this transparency is one of the foundations
          of my rule.
        consequences: []
        dailyChanges: []
        receivingVaribale: {fileID: 0}
      isFinalLine: 0
      nextSpeakerID: 0
    - line: If this leads to my downfall, so shall it be.
      choices:
      - conditionToShow: {fileID: 0}
        conditionToHide: {fileID: 0}
        choiceText: I will keep that in mind.
        responseToChoice: May you be successful in that.
        consequences: []
        dailyChanges: []
        receivingVaribale: {fileID: 0}
      isFinalLine: 0
      nextSpeakerID: 0
